Z||000010||Cooter||10-15-2001||07:59 PM||||Make an offer- the HO scale locomotive is there for size comparison. The car is a 1/8 scale with an OPS engine and complete receiver/servo system.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Dcp01685.jpg">  <BR>Bryce- when are you going to be in Oxford? Remember- that is getting close to home.<p>[This message has been edited by Cooter (edited 10-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||84Bill||10-15-2001||08:31 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by batt:<BR><B>what you guys are doing sounds fun. how would one learn what they need to do to drive/work on nicer r/c's. Another thing, it sounds as if r/cs are totally customizable, is this true?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah man R/C is fun! AND very customizable. Some guys spen thousands of dollars to trick out an R/C to look like a scale car or a replica od their own car can be built from scratch. It costs alot up front (good car and radio 350.00 fuel 25.00 a gallon 100.00 in misc parts and bearings) but you can also get a car and radio for about 150.00, after that the sky is the limit. <BR>SAS Performance Parts page is brand spanking new and I'm still developing it but theese guys can make just about anything you want from any metals you want, even titanium! So far the only titanium products they make are the brake rotors (costs 150.00 for 1 linear foot of 1 inch dia. round bar) but other parts will follow. <BR>Fun Fun Fun<BR>Here is a <A HREF="http://www.boonyer.com/boonyers/streams/Soupday.wmv" TARGET=_blank>video</A> of last years fun.||||reg||14
Z||000012||Pontiaddict||10-15-2001||09:43 PM||||I remember making a hovercraft out of a budwiser case and some spare rc car parts. <BR>I'll have to find that video.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Nashco||10-15-2001||11:06 PM||||Wow, interest, excellent <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>84bill:  Like I said, we <B>are</B> going for a 100+ mph car.  Oh, and since we're only using a one speed trans, the torque of a bigger motor will be an awesome advantage.  I read once a long article on the internet that went into depths about a car that Ferdinand Porsche had started designing before world war II that used a 44 liter v12 and a single speed transmission, in hopes of breaking a land speed record.  It was an excellent article explaining the advantages of more speeds in modern transmissions, but showing that if you have more power, it's wasted energy to shift.  Anyway, I can't find the article for the life of me, but here's a blurb to show I'm not pulling this out my butt:  <A HREF="http://members.tripod.com/~msherman/Porsche.story.html" TARGET=_blank>http://members.tripod.com/~msherman/Porsche.story.html</A> <P>Oh, and for the cooling...I said above how it will be a high speed car, so air is there, and I hope to build a body that will direct airflow exactly where it is needed, if it doesn't cool good enough as it is.<P>batt: Easy question...start by going to the supermarket or bookstore and reading all the magazines for RC cars..there's a ton.  That will point you in the right direction; they're really pretty easy if you just want to fiddle with them, but they can be very complex at times.<P>My7Fieros:  Are you willing to donate, or what is your asking price?  PM me if you want, and thanks in advance for helping out.<P>Cooter:  I'll talk to my buddy and see what he thinks.  I was hoping to meet you soon anyway, and this may be a good reason too <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Also, I put up a post in general looking for you; you were hooking me up with somebody that would do my exhaust a while ago, but I didn't get it done.  I'm back here in Oxford, and I *NEED* to get my exhaust done...here's a link: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/007638.html" TARGET=_blank>'bama exhaust?</A><P>Pontiaddict:  Care to share more, sounds like fun!  Hovercrafts rule <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I don't have any update on the car yet...we're going over ideas, and he's getting some parts this week.  Things will be a little clearer then.  The big hold up right now is the lack of a 90 power adapter.  He's looking around on ebay hoping to come across stuff..which he has...but nothing cheap in any sense of the word.<P>Thanks everybody...you're all helping me to get hooked..hehe <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<P>||||reg||1
